  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_005 (RNA-only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1. Image-only with resnet50 was very weak (0.208), but we have not yet tested whether adding image features to the strong RNA signal via fusion can provide complementary information. The key uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion improves over the best unimodal model, which is the central question of this study. Config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the minimal, logical extension of config_005: it keeps every RNA-side setting at its best-known value and adds only the image modality with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of adding image information to the strongest RNA pipeline. If it improves, we have a new best and a clear direction for exploring fusion type and image encoder. If it does not, we learn that resnet50 image features do not complement scvi RNA representations, redirecting effort toward either a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) or RNA-only refinements. Under the limited budget, this single experiment directly answers the highest-value question—does multimodal fusion help?—using the most validated component settings available."
}

